Bundled third-party code
------------------------
voice_app/opencc.full.js is the OpenCC-JS 1.4.2 browser build (nk2028/opencc-js, MIT License),
used for Traditional/Simplified Chinese conversion in the browser. Its license and the licenses of
the dictionary data it embeds (OpenCC data, Apache-2.0) are in voice_app/OPENCC_LICENSE.txt and
voice_app/OPENCC_THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md; the source and checksum are in voice_app/OPENCC_SOURCE.md.

Third-party software and models (not included in this repository)
------------------------------------------------------------------
Apart from the file above, this repository contains no third-party code or model weights.
setup.ps1 installs dependencies from their own distributions (PyPI, PyTorch) and downloads
models from Hugging Face; each remains under its own license, which you must comply with.
The main components and the licenses declared in their package metadata at the time of writing:

  NiceGUI                              MIT
  httpx                                BSD-3-Clause
  SoundCard                            BSD-3-Clause
  PyAV (av)                            BSD-3-Clause
  NumPy                                BSD-3-Clause
  PyTorch (torch)                      BSD-3-Clause
  Hugging Face transformers            Apache-2.0
  Hugging Face huggingface_hub         Apache-2.0
  safetensors                          Apache-2.0
  qwen-asr                             Apache-2.0

  Qwen/Qwen3-ASR-1.7B                  Apache-2.0 (model weights, downloaded at install time)
  Qwen/Qwen3-ForcedAligner-0.6B        Apache-2.0 (model weights, downloaded at install time)

The full list of installed packages is pinned in constraints.txt (UI environment) and
requirements-asr.txt (speech-recognition environment). Review the license of each package
before redistributing a bundled copy of an installed environment.

The proofreading step sends transcribed text to the OpenAI-compatible chat service you
configure; the model and service you choose are subject to their own terms.
